DTSTAMP:19700101T000000Z
DTSTART:20260413T115900Z
DTEND:20260413T125900Z
SUMMARY:[Artificial Life & Adaptive Systems][Complex Systems & Network Scie
 nce] ALIFE 2026 - Extended full-paper submission deadline
DESCRIPTION:Conference title: International Conference on Artificial Life\n
 Website: https://2026.alife.org/\nSource URL: https://2026.alife.org/call
 -for-papers/\nLocation: Waterloo\, Ontario\, Canada\nTopics: Artificial L
 ife & Adaptive Systems\, Complex Systems & Network Science\, Evolutionary
  Computation & Optimization\, Cognitive Science & Computational Cognition
 \nSize: L\nSubmission type: Full papers + non-archival abstracts\nConfide
 nce: confirmed\nLast checked date: 2026-10-08\nNotes: Historical baseline
 . Reviewed full papers appear in MIT Press open-access proceedings\; pres
 entation summaries and late-breaking abstracts are non-archival. The Apri
 l date was an extension of the original March 30 cutoff. Size is an edito
 rial estimate.\nScope: Artificial life and life-like processes in computa
 tional\, robotic and biological systems. Central questions concern emerge
 nce\, evolution\, adaptation\, embodied intelligence and cognition. Relev
 ant ML work studies adaptive agents\, evolutionary learning and computati
 onal models of living systems\; it is not a general-purpose AI conference
 .\nAdditional topics: Autonomous Agents & Multiagent Systems\, Control & 
 Robotics\, Machine Learning\nScope sources (2026): https://2026.alife.org
 /call-for-papers/\, https://alife.org/conference/alife-2027/\nScope last 
 checked: 2026-10-08
URL:https://2026.alife.org/call-for-papers/
END:VEVENT
