 & Chaos\, Complex Systems & Network Science\, Deep Representation Learnin
 g\, Control & Robotics\nSize: M\nSubmission type: Paper-based\nConfidence
 : confirmed\nLast checked date: 2026-10-06\nNotes: Annual IEICE NOLTA sym
 posium\; official final extensions supersede older April/July dates. Proc
 eedings papers\, with neural networks and deep AI explicitly in scope. De
 adline hours use estimated end-of-day AoE. Size is an editorial category.
 \nScope: Nonlinear theory and its applications\, centered on chaos\, bifu
 rcations\, oscillations\, synchronization\, nonlinear circuits\, and comp
 lex networks. Neural computation\, evolutionary algorithms\, control\, an
 d signal processing connect to this nonlinear-systems focus. Individual a
 pplication examples are not taken as additional specialist identities.\nA
 dditional topics: Signal Processing\, Evolutionary Computation & Optimiza
 tion\nScope sources (2026): https://nolta2026.org/\nScope last checked: 2
